# GENERATED by roto_mapper's maps_to_fl.py from its FL map files (maps_fl): don't
# edit by hand (edit the map in roto_mapper and regenerate).
#
# Default control maps for FL Studio's own plugins, for ROTO's PLUGIN mode. ROTO
# asks for one when the selected plugin has nothing mapped on any page (the
# map-empty byte of CONTROL_MAPPED_END); the script sends it with
# SET_DEFAULT_CTL. ROTO holds it in RAM only, so it updates with the script.
# LEARN starts from a blank plugin (the default is dropped; left with nothing
# learnt, the default comes back), and what's learnt is saved to ROTO and used
# from then on. CLEARing a control of the default saves the rest of it.
#
# Keyed by FL's name for the plugin (plugins.getPluginName, not the user's).
# A control: ctl (page * 8 + control), knob (else a switch), index and hash (the
# parameter's: name_hash of its name, 6 bytes), steps (a knob's N steps, 0 =
# continuous; a switch's positions), and optionally centre (a knob's centre
# detent), indents (a continuous knob's own detents, 0..127), push (a momentary
# switch), name (ROTO's label), colour, min / max (14-bit knob, 7-bit switch),
# ledOn / ledOff (palette indices).

